<urn:atm:triage:finding/AW-POOL-V9-QA-002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AW-POOL-V9-QA-002" ;
  triage:title "FIX-8's ReadLaneError::Storage preserves code but still drops the original AtmError cause on the round trip" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr's PR #1244 (A2, fix/aw-pool-read-migration) re-QA: AW-POOL-V9-FIX-8's fix (commit ba8ebc039, mailbox_reader.rs storage_error()) added ReadLaneError::Storage{code, message} and threads the AtmErrorCode correctly through From<ReadLaneError> for AtmError, but still drops the original AtmError's cause() (the raw SQLite driver failure text/source chain) on the round trip back to AtmError. Locations: crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/mailbox_reader.rs:162 (storage_error()), crates/atm-storage/src/contract.rs:396-441 (ReadLaneError enum and its From impl). Recommended fix: thread the original AtmError (or at least its cause/source) through ReadLaneError::Storage as well, e.g. add a boxed source field, so From<ReadLaneError> for AtmError can call .with_cause(...) using the original error's cause chain instead of only recovering the code." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-aw" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "rust-best-practices" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-06T03:15:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AWWriterPoolAudit ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-06T03:10:59Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
